  "goodToKnow": "Hiesig means local, belonging to here: die hiesige Bevölkerung, hiesige Produkte, der hiesige Dialekt. It's only used before a noun. Its partner is dortig (from there): die dortigen Behörden. Both are slightly formal; in speech, Germans say von hier or die Leute hier. As a noun, die Hiesigen means the locals. Regional pride in hiesige products, from beer to Spargel (asparagus), is strong in Germany."
